th ♠10, then immediately giving them the chance to beat ♥6 on the next lead. If they can beat ♥6, they win (they have 4 cards, maybe a bomb or rocket — none seen yet — but less likely).  \n\nActually, the remaining cards show no 2s or jokers left in deck (they were played earlier). That means no rockets and no 2s for bombs except maybe quad bombs using 4 of a rank (none seen).  \n\nGiven the small hand sizes, the biggest threat is the left player (4 cards) going out soon. If I pass now, they might play a pair or sequence I can’t beat with my two non-paired cards, and win.  \n\nThus, it’s safer to take control now with ♠10 — force them to have a higher single to beat me. If they don’t, I lead last card ♥6 and hope they can’t beat it.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": ["♠10"]}'}
